  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nFollowing one last shortwave trough affecting the region on Monday \nwith rain chances reaching beyond the Caprock, rain chances dry up\nfor Tuesday and Wednesday under drier and more stable southwest \nflow. This milder and drier theme for midweek looks short lived \nas the southern jet stream amplifies in response to deep troughing\noccupying the West Coast. Combined with a return of ample Pacific\nmoisture (including a potential tap from a tropical wave), this \npattern is favorable for another regional precip scenario by the \nfinal few days of October. No cold fronts are on the horizon \nanytime soon, and dewpoints hold in the 50s most days and nights. \nThis points to mild nightly lows with daily highs returning to \nnear-normal territory by Tuesday and remain so through Halloween.",
